   "source": [
    "# 13. ATTACKS BASED ON FILE AND PATH NAMES"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "5f875ba6-338c-4474-9f1b-514d60b897a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "These attacks occur when an attacker manipulates a file path\n",
    "in an HTTP request to access files outside the permitted directory.\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "1. PATH TRAVERSAL / DIRECTORY TRAVERSAL\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "The attacker uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "..\n",
    "\n",
    "`..` means \"parent directory\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "GET /../../secret.txt HTTP/1.1\n",
    "\n",
    "If the server does not properly validate the path, the attacker\n",
    "may access files outside the intended web directory.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Allowed directory:\n",
    "    /var/www/html/\n",
    "\n",
    "Attacker tries:\n",
    "    /var/www/html/../../etc/passwd\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "2. IMPACT\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "An attacker may gain access to:\n",
    "\n",
    "    • Configuration files\n",
    "    • Password/credential files\n",
    "    • System files\n",
    "    • Other sensitive resources\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "3. PREVENTION\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "The server should:\n",
    "\n",
    "    • Validate user-supplied paths\n",
    "    • Normalize/canonicalize paths\n",
    "    • Prevent `..` from escaping the allowed directory\n",
    "    • Restrict file access to the intended document root\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "MEMORY TRICK\n",
    "--------------------------------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "`..` → Go to parent directory\n",
    "\n",
    "Path Traversal → Attacker uses paths to go outside\n",
    "the allowed directory."
   ]
  },
